WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome back, everybody.
We're here with Alicia Keys!

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:05.801
-Hey!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:07.968
-You've done so many things,
so many cool things.

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:09.467
By the way, I can't wait
to talk about this

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:11.601
because this is
just the raddest.

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:14.200
It's awesome.
Yeah, I know, it's so fun.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.067
15 Grammys, best-selling author,

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:23.634
but also, you're into the --
in fashion, as well, Athleta.

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:25.400
-Yes.
-Yeah, talk to me about this.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.534
-So Athleta I love because
I'm actually a fan of Athleta

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:32.567
as a mom, as a person who likes
to work out, likes to meditate,

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:36.100
just be able to have that
kind of soft, sweet energy.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.767
But what I love about them
the most

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:39.801
is that they're all about
body consciousness

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:42.834
and body positivity
and body diversity.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:45.834
And so we created
a limited-edition collection

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:47.267
that we're doing together.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:51.367
And it goes from all the way up
to 3X in size,

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:53.634
which I think is so important
to be able to find yourself

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:54.901
in the store.
-Yeah.

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:57.934
-And it's all about
powerful colors and boldness

00:00:57.934 --> 00:01:01.200
and really empowering women
to feel incredible

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.467
so that you can throw on
your little fit, go to the gym,

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:06.434
take your kids to school,
go take a brunch,

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:09.634
and still be fresh and powerful
the whole time.

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:11.100
-Wait till you see it.
It looks so cool.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.667
I'm like, "Oh, how do you --"
I mean, it's awesome.

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:19.267
Go to athleta.com and check out
Alicia Keys, what you did.

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:20.901
And then can we just
talk about this?

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:22.434
This is so cool,
and I just told you this.

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:24.434
I had the book because
I knew you were coming on.

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.067
I went to the bookstore
this weekend.

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:27.234
Shout-out to BookHampton.

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:29.434
They had a big, big display
of your book.

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:31.067
-BookHampton!
-It looked great.

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:33.033
It was awesome.
And I was like --

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:35.667
It just -- And it popped out,
and I was there with my girls.

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:38.534
And I'm like, this is great,
what you're doing.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:40.467
-I love this.
This is a graphic novel.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.801
It's my first graphic novel.
I love it so much.

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:45.334
I think it's a beautiful way
to introduce kids

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:48.801
to just continue to fall in love
with words and reading,

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:52.234
and I've been so grateful to
have fallen in love with words.

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:54.901
And that's why I'm a songwriter
and why I'm a storyteller,

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:56.534
because I love words.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:58.434
So when you meet Lolo --
Her name is Lolo.

00:01:58.434 --> 00:01:59.968
She's from Brooklyn.

00:01:59.968 --> 00:02:03.367
She's raised by a single father,
who's also raising her brother.

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:04.868
Her mother is actually
not around.

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.934
As you read the story,
you'll find out why.

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:09.400
And her brother
was racially profiled

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.667
and attacked
by a police officer,

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:14.133
and she got so upset,
she wanted to protect him,

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:15.334
and she just didn't know
what to do,

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.200
and she realizes at that moment

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.267
that she has
these special powers,

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:23.434
this kinetic energy that could
actually hurt you very badly.

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:25.601
And she's trying to figure out,
"What do I do with this energy?

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:27.200
How do I harness it?
How do I use it?

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.367
Am I crazy?"

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:30.634
And the whole book
is really a metaphor

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:32.501
to the superpowers we all have

00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:35.434
and trying to find our way
to harness it.

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:37.367
-Wait till you see the reaction
you're going to get

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:41.133
from teenagers and kids
and parents reading it.

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:43.934
Watching a kid read your stuff,
it's like --

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:45.467
-It's crazy.
-It's game-changing.

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.968
You go, "Wow, we're so lucky to
be able to do stuff like this."

00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:49.434
But good on you for doing this.

00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:53.033
-And the song "Girl on Fire" has
been such a powerful statement,

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:55.801
and I wrote it
when I didn't feel on fire.

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:57.701
I wrote it when I felt like
I couldn't make it,

00:02:57.701 --> 00:03:01.334
when I saw my friends
and my family members, as women,

00:03:01.334 --> 00:03:03.934
feeling defeated,
and reminding us

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:06.534
that there is nothing that
stops us, we are on fire.

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:08.634
And so to see this transform
into a book

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:11.267
that can hopefully do that
for so many others is like --

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:12.868
I'm super grateful.

00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:15.367
-That's what I'm talking about.
That is Alicia Keys.

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:17.534
Thank you so much
for being here in person.

00:03:17.534 --> 00:03:19.267
I missed you!
I missed you, bud.

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:21.767
Congrats on everything.
Alicia Keys, everybody.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.133
"Girl on Fire" is out now.

